Not at all, I can read it just fine.

154
00:08:59,508 --> 00:09:05,508
「Jump King」は、プレイヤーが高いたものを登らなければならない、難易度の高い2Dプラットフォーマーゲームです！
"Jump King" is a high-difficulty 2D platformer game where the player must climb a tall tower!

155
00:09:05,808 --> 00:09:11,208
「ジャンプ」ボタンを押すと、ジャンプの方向を変更できなくなるため、その難易度の高い...
Because you cannot change jump direction once you press the "Jump" button, its difficulty is high...

156
00:09:11,208 --> 00:09:14,208
悪名高いゲームとなっております！
It is infamous for its high difficulty!

157
00:09:14,208 --> 00:09:15,508
超ムズですのじゃ。
It's super hard.

158
00:09:15,508 --> 00:09:20,008
「ジャンプ」ボタンを長押しする時間によって、ジャンプの勢いが変わるようになっております！
Depending on how long you hold down the "Jump" button, the momentum of the jump changes!

159
00:09:20,008 --> 00:09:22,008
時間によって変わるらしいのじゃ。
Apparently it changes depending on the timing.

160
00:09:22,008 --> 00:09:24,508
Yes, difficult game. Very hard.

161
00:09:25,008 --> 00:09:26,508
ムズムズゲーム。
A super hard game.

162
00:09:26,508 --> 00:09:31,008
いや、本当に難しい。時間でね、ピョンとか... 小ジャンプとか中ジャンプとか...
No, really hard. Depending on the timing, like hop... small jump or medium jump...

163
00:09:31,008 --> 00:09:33,008
わしがさっき言ってたやつじゃん！
That's what I was talking about earlier!

164
00:09:33,008 --> 00:09:35,808
あっちちで使い分けてたやつじゃの。
The one I was using with "achichi".

165
00:09:36,008 --> 00:09:41,008
Very difficult! But today we have specific rules for this...

166
00:09:41,008 --> 00:09:42,508
ルールが...
The rules...

167
00:09:42,508 --> 00:09:44,008
...for this race!

168
00:09:44,008 --> 00:09:45,008
このレースでは...
In this race...

169
00:09:45,008 --> 00:09:49,008
All racers will start at the very bottom of the map with their timers set to 0.

170
00:09:49,008 --> 00:09:51,008
一番最初のスタートしたところから始めて...
Starting from the very bottom starting point...

171
00:09:51,008 --> 00:09:54,008
Until the timer hits 1 hour, our racers will need to jump as high as they possibly can.

172
00:09:54,008 --> 00:09:56,008
1時間でどこまで行けるか...
How far they can go in 1 hour...

173
00:09:56,008 --> 00:09:59,808
However, it's easy to fall down very far, so they'll need to adapt!

174
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:03,966
...to adapt. I know some of them have been practicing and some have not, which will make it even more fun.

175
00:10:04,136 --> 00:10:07,856
「練習してる人もいれば、しない人もいる大会ですよ」と。
Some have practiced, some haven't - that's this tournament for you!

176
00:10:08,536 --> 00:10:15,556
「ということでなのじゃ！『すべてのレーサーはマップの最下部からスタートし、タイマーは00:00:00に設定されます。』」
So here it is! 'All racers will start at the very bottom of the map, with their timers set to 00:00:00.'

177
00:10:15,556 --> 00:10:21,066
『タイマーが1時間になるまでに、レーサーたちはできるだけ高くジャンプしなければなりません。』
'Until the timer hits 1 hour, racers will need to jump as high up as they possibly can!'

178
00:10:21,066 --> 00:10:23,776
できるだけ高くね！
Jump as high as possible!

179
00:10:23,216 --> 00:10:29,126
『しかし、あっという間に下まで落ちてしまうこともあるので、状況に応じて対応していく必要があります！』
'However, it's easy to fall down very far, so they'll need to adapt!'

180
00:10:29,416 --> 00:10:34,216
たぶん1時間後の現在地って言ったかな、最高地点というより。
I think she meant current position after 1 hour, rather than the highest point reached.

181
00:10:34,016 --> 00:10:36,516
So, yeah... it's a bit of a gamble.

182
00:10:36,216 --> 00:10:41,016
どこまで行けるか、みたいな。どこまでジャンプしていくか、それとも止まっておくか、みたいなのも…
Like "how far can I get?" Whether to keep jumping or stay put...

183
00:10:41,016 --> 00:10:45,016
たしかに！結構、上位に入るには考えなきゃいけないのかなと。
True! To make it to the top ranks, you might really have to think about it.

184
00:10:44,816 --> 00:10:48,516
「ここまで行けたならもういいか」って止まって雑談したっていいからね。どこで止まるか。
You could even stop and chat, thinking "I made it this far, so I'm good." Where to stop?

185
00:10:48,516 --> 00:10:51,516
それも含めて計算らしいですのじゃ！
Calculating all of that is part of it!

186
00:10:50,416 --> 00:10:53,016
That last 10 minutes is gonna be a little scary maybe...

187
00:10:52,416 --> 00:10:57,016
最後の10分で落下になっちゃったみたいなこと、一番下行っちゃったらね、意味ないですのでね！
If you end up falling to the very bottom in the last 10 minutes, it'd be all for nothing!

188
00:10:57,016 --> 00:10:59,016
Yeah, it's a gamble, man!

189
00:10:58,516 --> 00:11:00,816
そう！ギャンブル！本当にギャンブルです！
Right! A gamble! It really is a gamble!

190
00:11:00,616 --> 00:11:04,016
大会らしいですのじゃ！戦略が！
Very fitting for a tournament! Strategy is key!

191
00:11:02,316 --> 00:11:04,516
Be careful, everyone!

192
00:11:04,516 --> 00:11:18,516
When time is up, racers will take a screenshot of their last position. We'll use that screenshot to decide who has officially climbed the farthest up the tower! Please note: It's okay if the timer has run a bit farther than 1 hour as long as the contestant has stopped moving at 01:00:00.

193
00:11:18,516 --> 00:11:27,516
I know sometimes, you know, you're excited, you jump... and then you screenshot. As long as they stopped moving 1 hour in, it's totally fine.

194
00:11:29,016 --> 00:11:34,516
『制限時間が終了したら、参加者は最後の位置のスクリーンショットを撮影していただきます。』
'When time is up, racers will take a screenshot of their last position.'

195
00:11:34,516 --> 00:11:40,816
『このスクリーンショットをもとに、塔を最も高く登り切った参加者を正式に決定します。』
'We'll use that screenshot to decide who has officially climbed the farthest up the tower.'

196
00:11:41,016 --> 00:11:54,016
『1時間の時点で参加者が動きを止めている限り、タイマーが1時間を少し超えていても問題ないので、1時間経った時に一旦止まっていただけると嬉しいです！』
'As long as the contestant has stopped moving at 1 hour, it's okay if the timer has run a bit past 1 hour, so we'd appreciate it if you could pause when 1 hour passes!'

197
00:11:54,016 --> 00:11:56,516
そこをスクリーンショットして送ってください！
Please take a screenshot of that position and send it over!

198
00:11:56,816 --> 00:12:00,016
あ！推しら、今のうちにわしの動画、高評価を押してくれると嬉しいのじゃ！
Ah! Fans, while you're at it, I'd be happy if you pressed like on my stream!

199
00:12:00,016 --> 00:12:12,516
Completion of the game is not required, nor is it likely, but in the event a racer completes the game, they will start a new game right away upon reaching the babe at the top, and continue climbing once again until the timer hits 01:00:00.

200
00:12:13,016 --> 00:12:24,016
Again, it's unlikely, you know. This is just for newbies, and you know, I didn't want to put them through 2 hours of racing, or even 3. I think 1 is enough to get the general idea of how they're doing...

201
00:12:26,516 --> 00:12:29,516
...yes, if someone does complete it, they will have to start again.

202
00:12:29,816 --> 00:12:34,816
『ゲームをクリアする必要はなく、そもそもクリアできる可能性はとても低いですが…』
'Completion of the game is not required, nor is it likely...'

203
00:12:34,816 --> 00:12:47,016
『万が一レーサーがゲームをクリアした場合は、頂上の美女に到達するとすぐに新しいゲームを開始し、タイマーが01:00:00になるまで再度登り続けてください。』
'...but in the event a racer completes the game, they will start a new game right away upon reaching the babe at the top, and continue climbing once again until the timer hits 01:00:00.'

204
00:12:43,016 --> 00:12:47,016
2周目もOKらしいのじゃ！
Looks like a 2nd loop is allowed!

205
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:54,016
クリアできたらいいらしい！わし、先紀すっごい頑張ったのに、5%しか進んでなかったのじゃ！
Great if anyone can clear it! Though last time I tried super hard, I only made 5% progress!

206
00:12:54,016 --> 00:12:59,016
低いですけど、まあ奇跡が起こるかもしれませんからね！
It's low, but a miracle might happen after all!

207
00:12:59,516 --> 00:13:14,016
All of today's racers are brand new racers, and they have only had 5 days to practice. We'll start the race when Mori says 'Go!'. The top 3 jumpers will receive prizes! May the next Jump King emerge victorious!

208
00:13:14,016 --> 00:13:17,516
告知されてから練習OKです、みたい感じだったから…
Since practice was allowed after it was announced...

209
00:13:17,516 --> 00:13:26,016
『今日の出演者は全員初めてレースに参加する選手たちで、練習期間はわずか5日間しかありませんでした！』
'All of today's racers are brand new racers, and they have only had 5 days to practice!'

210
00:13:26,016 --> 00:13:28,516
『カリオペ先輩が「GO！」と合図を出したらレースを開始します！』
'We'll start the race when Calliope-senpai says "Go!"'

211
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:32,016
これ今あれだな、テスト勉強してないと言ってる人みたい…
This sounds like someone claiming they didn't study for a test...

212
00:13:31,016 --> 00:13:40,016
『上位3名のジャンパーには豪華な賞品が贈られます！新たなジャンプキングの伝説の幕開けを楽しみにしております！』
'The top 3 jumpers will receive luxurious prizes! Looking forward to the dawn of a new Jump King legend!'

213
00:13:40,016 --> 00:13:43,016
豪華賞品がもらえるのですね！
So we get luxurious prizes!

214
00:13:43,016 --> 00:13:45,516
豪華賞品！いただいてもよろしいのか…！
Luxurious prizes! May I really receive one...!

215
00:13:45,516 --> 00:13:49,016
楽しみ！優越感！
Looking forward to it! Superiority!

216
00:13:49,016 --> 00:13:52,516
何がもらえるんだろう？トロフィーとかかな？
I wonder what we'll get? Maybe a trophy or something?

217
00:13:53,016 --> 00:14:08,016
Now before we get started, we have a special message to share with all of you guys today! First, though, I will go ahead and let the racers know... well, actually, we'll probably go ahead and start at 20. Just a moment, please, while I send everybody the message. 19:20...

218
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:16,816
はい！7時20分よりレース始める感じになる気がしますのじゃ！
Yes! Feels like the race will start from 7:20!

219
00:14:17,016 --> 00:14:20,516
So at 20, we will start! Special message!

220
00:14:20,516 --> 00:14:24,016
特別メッセージ！特別メッセージですか？どなたでしょうか？
Special message! A special message? Who could it be?

221
00:14:24,016 --> 00:14:26,216
伝説の方ですか？
Is it from the legend?

222
00:14:26,216 --> 00:14:30,016
We received a very special message, everyone, from the Jump King!

223
00:14:28,016 --> 00:14:31,516
伝説の方からメッセージもらいました！
We got a message from the legendary person!

224
00:14:31,516 --> 00:14:41,016
From the Jump King herself! So, the Jump King has a message for all of today's racers!

225
00:14:41,016 --> 00:14:43,016
じゃじゃーん！
Tada!

226
00:14:43,016 --> 00:14:48,516
「ホロレースに参加の皆さん、お疲れ様です！風真いろはです！」
"To everyone participating in the Holorace, good work! This is Kazama Iroha!"

227
00:14:48,516 --> 00:14:50,516
Wow, Jump King master!

228
00:14:50,516 --> 00:14:59,016
「本日は Jump King を愛する者として皆さんにアドバイスをしに来ました！」
"Today, as a lover of Jump King, I've come to give you all some advice!"

229
00:14:58,216 --> 00:15:00,016
アドバイス来た！来た来た来た！
Advice is here! It's here, it's here, it's here!

230
00:15:00,048 --> 00:15:02,193
I'll give you some advice.

231
00:15:02,754 --> 00:15:04,633
このゲームのポイントはですね...
The key to this game...

232
00:15:04,834 --> 00:15:05,498
はい。
Yes.

233
00:15:05,794 --> 00:15:07,524
チル！
Chill!

234
00:15:07,752 --> 00:15:09,943
チル？ え？ まぁまぁまぁ、確かに...
Chill? Huh? Well, that's true...

235
00:15:10,074 --> 00:15:11,782
今日、いろは先輩の...
Today, Iroha-senpai's...

236
00:15:12,184 --> 00:15:13,463
朝配信ちょっと見たけど...
I watched a bit of her morning stream...

237
00:15:13,654 --> 00:15:16,874
「チル」って言いながらやってたのじゃん。確かに。
...and she was saying "Chill" while playing. True.

238
00:15:17,174 --> 00:15:20,324
The key to this game is chill. Yes, chill.

239
00:15:20,754 --> 00:15:23,303
If you fall, just climb back up.

240
00:15:23,654 --> 00:15:26,502
初心者、再現性あるのかな...
I wonder if beginners can actually reproduce that...

241
00:15:26,674 --> 00:15:27,784
Woah...

242
00:15:28,193 --> 00:15:30,364
上手い人がチルしながらやるのはありだけど...
It's fine for good players to chill, but...

243
00:15:30,424 --> 00:15:33,874
諦めず、全力で楽しんでください！
Don't give up, and have fun with all your heart!

244
00:15:33,934 --> 00:15:37,363
ありがとうのじゃー！ 頑張るのじゃー！
Thank you so much! I'll do my best!

245
00:15:37,914 --> 00:15:41,253
それでは皆さん、グッドラックでござる！
Well then, good luck to everyone!

246
00:15:41,554 --> 00:15:44,224
あっきーのじゃー！ ござるー！
Akki-noja! Gozaru!

247
00:15:44,274 --> 00:15:48,363
さすがねー。重みのある言葉、素晴らしいお言葉でしたねー。
As expected. Those were weighty, wonderful words.

248
00:15:48,424 --> 00:15:52,024
わぁー、なるほどー。ジャンプキング、ありがとうございましたー。
Wow, I see. Jump King, thank you very much.

249
00:15:52,104 --> 00:15:55,224
言葉になかったぞ、いろは先輩... 気のせいかな...
Wait, Iroha-senpai didn't say that in the message... Was I hearing things...?

250
00:15:55,363 --> 00:15:59,024
チル... チルでキーボード壊れるのかな？ 本当にアドバイスはチルなのか？
Chill... Does "chill" mean breaking your keyboard? Is the advice really just "chill"?

251
00:15:59,094 --> 00:16:03,024
いろはちゃん本当にありがとうね。優しい言葉... キーボード壊さなきゃ始まらない気がし...
Iroha-chan, thank you so much for those kind words... I feel like if I don't break the keyboard...

252
00:16:03,974 --> 00:16:06,693
...they can get. So thank you so much.

253
00:16:07,434 --> 00:16:11,474
Now then, it looks like it might be just about time to get right into it...

254
00:16:11,774 --> 00:16:15,524
閉じる... 閉じる...
Close... Close...

255
00:16:15,853 --> 00:16:18,524
We'll start at 20, shall we?

256
00:16:18,914 --> 00:16:21,024
はい、20分... 20分から...
Yes, 20 minutes... starting from 20 minutes...

257
00:16:21,104 --> 00:16:24,524
19時20分ぐらい、はい、スタートします。
We'll start around 19:20.

258
00:16:24,654 --> 00:16:26,524
え、じゃあもうすぐスタートなんじゃない？
Eh, then isn't the start super soon?

259
00:16:26,674 --> 00:16:29,802
はい、よろしくお願いします！
Yes, best of luck!

260
00:16:29,874 --> 00:16:31,524
はい！ 頑張りますのじゃー！
Yes! I'll do my best!

261
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:34,524
本当に楽しみだ、マジで。ドキドキワクワクです。
I'm really looking forward to this, honestly. It's so exciting.

262
00:16:34,584 --> 00:16:37,024
いけるかなー... どうなるかなー...
I wonder if I can do it... How will it go...?

263
00:16:37,074 --> 00:16:40,524
や、やっぱり同期の配信は見れてて...
Well, I was able to watch my genmates' streams...

264
00:16:40,584 --> 00:16:44,224
結局落ちやすい... キョーコとそぴあの配信はちらっと見たんじゃけど...
I took a quick look at Kyoko's and Sopia's streams...

265
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:48,913
その他の参加者の先輩方の配信は... こうやるのが大事な気がしますねー。
but for the other participating senpai...

266
00:16:48,974 --> 00:16:52,513
敵、敵だから... 敵のを見るのって良くないかなみたいな...
...they're rivals, so I thought watching rivals might not be good...

267
00:16:52,574 --> 00:16:56,524
ちょっと良くないかなと思って見ないようにしていて...
So I tried not to watch them...

268
00:16:56,594 --> 00:16:59,024
だから、実際他の先輩がどれくらいできるか...
...so I don't really know how well the other senpais can play...

269
00:16:59,084 --> 00:17:02,024
ちなみに、リオナちゃんは... ソピアとキョーコがどれくらいできるかは大体わかってるんだけど...
I pretty much know how well Sopia and Kyoko can play...

270
00:17:02,084 --> 00:17:06,024
他の方がどれくらいできるかを分かっておらず...
...but I don't know about the others...

271
00:17:06,104 --> 00:17:08,524
どれくらい行けるかな...
I wonder how far I can go...

272
00:17:08,584 --> 00:17:11,824
イライラしてくる可能性はあるんですけど...
There's a chance you'll get frustrated, but...

273
00:17:11,874 --> 00:17:14,824
1時間だったら、とにかく早く上がる！
If it's 1 hour, just climb fast!

274
00:17:14,874 --> 00:17:17,524
早く上がる！ 当たり前で笑った！
Climb fast! That's so obvious, it made me laugh!

275
00:17:17,574 --> 00:17:20,524
落ち着いて早く上がる！ 理想だ！
Stay calm and climb fast! That's the ideal!

276
00:17:20,584 --> 00:17:24,024
覚えゲーだと思うので... 覚えゲー！
I think it's a memory game... A memory game!

277
00:17:24,074 --> 00:17:28,524
大ジャンプだったかな、中ジャンプだったかな、みたいなのをできるだけ覚えておくといいかも...
Remembering if it was a big jump or medium jump as much as possible might help...

278
00:17:28,584 --> 00:17:34,524
あれね！ 大ジャンプはあっちめらー！ で、中ジャンプはあっちめ！ で、小ジャンプはあっち！
Right! Big jump is "Achimera~!", medium jump is "Achime!", and small jump is "Achi!"

279
00:17:34,584 --> 00:17:37,524
練習の時間があまりなかったかな...
Maybe there wasn't much time to practice...

280
00:17:37,584 --> 00:17:40,524
そうですよね、何回もやるしかないですからね。 何回もやるしかない。
That's true, you just have to do it over and over. Just gotta keep trying.

281
00:17:40,584 --> 00:17:47,024
いやそう、何回もやるしかない覚えゲーのジャンプキングにおいて、正直昨日から始めたのじゃかなり不利なんじゃが...
Yeah, in a memorization game like Jump King where you just have to keep trying, starting yesterday puts me at quite a disadvantage...

282
00:17:47,074 --> 00:17:51,524
みんなのボイスを聞きに行く... 不利ではありますが...
...going around to listen to everyone's voice... It is a disadvantage, but...

283
00:17:51,574 --> 00:17:55,024
ありますが... 頑張るのじゃ！
...even so... I'll do my best!

284
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:57,824
そうしますね。ちょっと邪魔しますね、私たち。
We'll do that then. We'll pop in to bother you guys a bit.

285
00:17:57,874 --> 00:18:00,824
そう！ なんか入る、入りに来てくださるらしい！
Right! Apparently they're gonna drop into our voice chats!

286
00:18:00,874 --> 00:18:05,024
お喋りに来てくださいらしいのじゃん。 ちょっと意地悪な私たち...
They said they're coming to chat. We're being a little mean...

287
00:18:05,074 --> 00:18:09,524
楽しみですね！ ドキドキワクワクです...
I'm looking forward to it! I'm so excited...

288
00:18:09,574 --> 00:18:13,024
集中のために、よいしょ...
For the sake of concentration... here we go...

289
00:18:13,084 --> 00:18:18,024
あと2分です。皆さんドキドキ... じゃあ、そろそろ先輩の配信を閉じて...
2 minutes left. Everyone's heart is pounding... Alright, time to close senpai's stream...

290
00:18:18,074 --> 00:18:22,524
ボスになりたいから... 閉じて... えーっと、ゲーム画面を開こうかな！
Close... Um, let's open the game screen!

291
00:18:22,584 --> 00:18:26,524
カリオペ... 頑張ってね...
Calliope... Good luck...

292
