01:38:29,952 --> 01:38:37,652
なかなかいい所が見つからなくてさ、困ってたの！ おすすめまで教えてもらえるとの噂... 嬉しいのじゃー！
I couldn't find a good place and was struggling! I heard a rumor they might even recommend a place... I'm so happy~!

1779
01:38:38,352 --> 01:38:41,352
そしてキョーコ... ウィナー！
And Kyoko... winner!

1780
01:38:41,352 --> 01:38:45,152
1位キョーコ！ すごい！
1st place is Kyoko! Awesome!

1781
01:38:45,152 --> 01:38:48,652
Yeah! We have 1st place!

1782
01:38:48,652 --> 01:38:51,652
マジマジ！ マジませーん！
For real, for real! No way!

1783
01:38:51,652 --> 01:38:56,652
でけぇ声！ 1位おめでとー！ すごいキョーコー！
So loud! Congrats on 1st place! Awesome, Kyoko~!

1784
01:38:56,652 --> 01:39:00,152
You did it! How does it feel?

1785
01:39:00,152 --> 01:39:05,652
I feel so good! Yeah, I feel so good! Like, not only I won, but I played really well, too!

1786
01:39:03,652 --> 01:39:05,652
声がデカい！
Her voice is so loud!

1787
01:39:05,652 --> 01:39:10,152
すごいキョーコ！
Kyoko is amazing!

1788
01:39:10,152 --> 01:39:13,152
You actually reached the highest point ever!

1789
01:39:13,152 --> 01:39:17,952
え！ 今までで一番高いらしい！ すごい！
Eh! Apparently that was her highest point ever! Awesome!

1790
01:39:20,652 --> 01:39:27,652
本番で一番高いポイント！ え、わしとキョーコ一緒！ 本番に強いタイプなんじゃない、両方とも！
Her highest score in the actual match! Eh, Kyoko and I are the same! Maybe we're both the type that performs well when it counts!

1791
01:39:30,652 --> 01:39:36,652
やっぱさ、アソビまわり隊さ、デビュー前さ、実はゲームユニットなんじゃないかみたいなさ、噂あったけどさ...
You know, before Asobi☆Mawaritai!'s debut, there were rumors like 'aren't they actually a gaming unit?'...

1792
01:39:36,652 --> 01:39:41,352
アソビまわり隊、もしやゲームユニット... ゲームチームか？！
Could Asobi☆Mawaritai! actually be a gaming unit... a gaming team?!

1793
01:39:41,352 --> 01:39:46,952
You get this special golden Jump King trophy... with a big Jump King crown on...

1794
01:39:46,952 --> 01:39:49,152
いいなー！ 金色のトロフィーじゃ！
How nice~! A gold trophy!

1795
01:39:49,152 --> 01:39:54,152
Yes, of course! And we also have a very special 1st place gift...

1796
01:39:54,152 --> 01:39:58,152
お！ ベリースペシャルファーストプライスギフトは何なんじゃ？
Oh! What is the very special 1st place gift?

1797
01:39:58,152 --> 01:40:00,152
Ta-da! Spa day with a friend!

1798
01:40:00,160 --> 01:40:05,160
...made the best choice! Spa day with a friend! Spa day package for two people!

1799
01:40:01,160 --> 01:40:05,760
2名様用 Spa day package... 2 people!
For 2 people... Spa day package... 2 people!

1800
01:40:06,060 --> 01:40:10,160
So that means you can take a friend for a full spa day together!

1801
01:40:10,060 --> 01:40:11,860
すごい！
Amazing!

1802
01:40:12,460 --> 01:40:16,760
え、スパデイパッケージってことはさ、マッサージだけじゃないってこと…
Wait, a spa day package means it's not just a massage, right?

1803
01:40:16,860 --> 01:40:18,960
You can go together!

1804
01:40:19,060 --> 01:40:23,360
丸一日、丸一日やれるってことですか？これ、スパを。
Does this mean we get a full day... a full day of spa treatments?

1805
01:40:23,260 --> 01:40:25,560
うん、すごいですよ。
Yeah, it's amazing.

1806
01:40:24,560 --> 01:40:27,360
2回勝った！
Won twice!

1807
01:40:27,060 --> 01:40:30,160
すごいねー！おめでとうー！
That's awesome! Congratulations!

1808
01:40:29,960 --> 01:40:33,360
2名様まで連れて行ってもらえるらしい！
Apparently, she can bring up to two people!

1809
01:40:34,360 --> 01:40:40,560
...to treat their eyes, and enjoy a trophy as well, and yeah, congrats!

1810
01:40:40,560 --> 01:40:43,160
素晴らしかった！お疲れー！
That was wonderful! Great job!

1811
01:40:41,460 --> 01:40:44,960
素晴らしかった！お疲れー！
That was wonderful! Great job!

1812
01:40:43,260 --> 01:40:44,860
Thank you so much!

1813
01:40:44,360 --> 01:40:46,460
ありがとうございます、のじゃちゃん！
Thank you very much, Noja-chan!

1814
01:40:46,060 --> 01:40:49,360
自分が行けると思ってる！行けると思ってる！
I bet she thinks she can go! She thinks she can go!

1815
01:40:48,460 --> 01:40:50,960
Riona is...

1816
01:40:49,560 --> 01:40:58,360
今日わしのこと好きじゃ... 今日わしのこと好きだからきっとわしのこと誘ってくれると思う！
Today she likes me... Today she likes me, so I'm sure she'll invite me!

1817
01:40:55,760 --> 01:41:00,260
Okay, that's it for the winners, yatta! However...
Okay, that's it for the winners, yay! However...

1818
01:40:59,960 --> 01:41:01,960
いい高ーい！
Nice and high!

1819
01:41:02,660 --> 01:41:05,260
お、あ、そうですね。言ってたけど。
Oh, ah, that's right. As we said before.

1820
01:41:05,260 --> 01:41:11,060
We have a special consolation prize for everybody that made it to the sewers!

1821
01:41:10,060 --> 01:41:11,960
お、参加賞！
Oh, participation prize!

1822
01:41:11,760 --> 01:41:13,360
Ta-da!

1823
01:41:12,160 --> 01:41:13,460
じゃんジャン！
Ta-da!

1824
01:41:13,260 --> 01:41:18,160
A gift card to the best American-style BBQ in Tokyo! Is my opinion though, in my opinion, but...

1825
01:41:14,460 --> 01:41:19,060
何ー？！
What?!

1826
01:41:20,360 --> 01:41:21,560
Most delicious!

1827
01:41:21,060 --> 01:41:26,660
これはあれですか？下水に行った方のプレゼントとして…
Is this... a gift for those who made it to the sewers?

1828
01:41:25,160 --> 01:41:27,660
はい！はい！
Yes! Yes!

1829
01:41:26,960 --> 01:41:32,960
カリオペ先輩のお気に入りのバーベキュー店のギフトカードがプレゼントされるようです！
Apparently, gift cards to Calliope-senpai's favorite BBQ joint are being given as prizes!

1830
01:41:29,960 --> 01:41:33,560
えぇー！
Ehhh?!

1831
01:41:31,560 --> 01:41:34,860
下水まで行った方、おめでとうございます！
Congratulations to everyone who made it to the sewers!

1832
01:41:33,860 --> 01:41:34,860
Yay!

1833
01:41:34,660 --> 01:41:36,860
下水まで行った人に！
To everyone who reached the sewers!

1834
01:41:36,260 --> 01:41:44,360
...dinner. However, this is only for the people... this is for everybody else who did not win. First, second place...

1835
01:41:43,860 --> 01:41:48,460
人たちは、まあ、既にあのプレゼントもらいましたから…
Those people already received their prizes, so...

1836
01:41:47,460 --> 01:41:51,060
あ、ダメらしい。わしはバーベキューダメ。
Ah, guess I can't. I don't get the BBQ.

1837
01:41:48,560 --> 01:41:50,560
トップ3以外もらいました。
Everyone outside the top 3 gets it.

1838
01:41:50,660 --> 01:42:00,760
わしはバーベキューダメ... さすがにご強欲か。マッサージの上にあの肉まで行くとなるとさすがに... さすがにご強欲か。
I can't get BBQ... I guess that would be too greedy. On top of a massage, getting meat too would be... I guess that's being too greedy.

1839
01:41:59,960 --> 01:42:07,160
BBQ for... Yes, yes! And just to clarify this, for everybody who reached the sewers, not everybody who ended in the sewers.

1840
01:42:07,260 --> 01:42:14,460
下水まで行ったらゲットです！終わりの場所ちょっとあの... 落ちたら大丈夫です。
If you reached the sewers, you get it! Even if you fell near the end, it's fine.

1841
01:42:14,060 --> 01:42:19,560
1回でも下水に行ってたら... 1回でも下水に到達してたらもらえる！
Even if you reached the sewers just once... As long as you hit the sewers at least once, you get it!

1842
01:42:19,160 --> 01:42:22,460
え、すごいのじゃー！すごい！
Eh, that's amazing! Amazing!

1843
01:42:22,160 --> 01:42:32,560
And as for people who did not make it to the sewers area... 下水まで行ってなかった人たちには... Calliopeはまだ多分何かあげたいと思うから、ちょっと考えています。
And as for people who did not make it to the sewers area... For those who didn't reach the sewers, Calliope might still want to give them something, so I'm thinking about it.

1844
01:42:32,660 --> 01:42:40,860
もしかしたら日々だけかもしれないんで、私が焼いたお肉の1枚をトングとかで掴んでお口にあげたいと思います。
It might just be small, so I'd like to take a piece of meat I grilled with tongs and feed it to them.

1845
01:42:41,860 --> 01:42:45,060
焼いた肉持っていきます、1枚。
I'll bring them one piece of grilled meat.

1846
01:42:45,060 --> 01:42:56,960
あのさ、下水まで行ってバーベキューってことはさ、マッサージ相当いいとこなんじゃないの、これ？
Hey, if reaching the sewers gets you BBQ, doesn't that mean this massage is somewhere really high-end?

1847
01:42:48,460 --> 01:42:53,460
リオナちゃん、ありがとうございました！嬉しい！
"Riona-chan, thank you so much!" I'm so glad!

1848
01:42:53,260 --> 01:42:57,560
相当いいマッサージなんじゃない？なんか、わしの想像するさ...
Isn't it a super high-class massage? Like, what I'm imagining...

1849
01:42:55,860 --> 01:42:58,360
This is high quality!

1850
01:42:58,060 --> 01:43:04,360
店員さんがめっちゃお仕事何されてるんですか？みたいに話しかけてきてさ...
...is the staff talking to you like, "So what kind of work do you do?"...

1851
01:43:02,960 --> 01:43:08,660
あと、私 Calliope 1人で行ったら全然つまらないと思うから...
Also, if I, Calliope, went alone, I think it wouldn't be fun at all...

1852
01:43:04,260 --> 01:43:10,260
どこにでもあるショッピングモールにあるチェーン店的な感じじゃないんじゃないの、もしかして？
Wouldn't it be different from those chain stores in regular shopping malls?

1853
01:43:08,660 --> 01:43:10,660
高クオリティのやつ。
High quality stuff.

1854
01:43:11,060 --> 01:43:16,960
めっちゃセレブ向けみたいな感じなんじゃないの、これ？わしそんなとこ行ったことないのじゃ！
Isn't this like something made for rich celebs? I've never been to a place like that!

1855
01:43:14,560 --> 01:43:18,360
Yeah! Yeah! So let's go, I'll take everybody.

1856
01:43:17,460 --> 01:43:21,060
どこにでもあるチェーン店のしか行ったことない！
I've only ever been to chain stores you see anywhere!

1857
01:43:20,960 --> 01:43:23,160
ちょっと待って...
Wait a minute...

1858
01:43:23,160 --> 01:43:27,160
えぇー！すごいんじゃないの？
Ehhh?! Isn't that amazing?

1859
01:43:25,960 --> 01:43:36,660
主催の挨拶もしたいので、行けた方は1つのチャットに集まっていただければ嬉しいです。お願いします。
I'd like to do the host's closing remarks, so if everyone who participated could gather in one Discord voice channel, that would be great. Please.

1860
01:43:35,460 --> 01:43:39,060
ボイスチャットに行ってきますのじゃ！よいしょ！よいしょ！
I'm heading to the voice chat! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

1861
01:43:43,860 --> 01:43:45,460
Okay, all right.

1862
01:43:44,660 --> 01:43:48,060
あ、入りますね！みんな入ります！
Ah, they're entering! Everyone's coming in!

1863
01:43:47,460 --> 01:43:48,960
のじゃー！
Noja~!

1864
01:43:48,760 --> 01:43:51,760
Hello, hello! Everyone's here!

1865
01:43:51,760 --> 01:43:53,760
Hi, guys!

1866
01:43:53,560 --> 01:43:58,360
よく出来た！ / お疲れ様ー！
You all did so well! / Good work, everyone!

1867
01:43:56,960 --> 01:43:59,360
のじゃー！
Noja~!

1868
01:44:05,260 --> 01:44:10,060
ねぇ、お疲れ様です！え、みなさん、本当に良く出来たよ！
Hey, good work! Everyone did so well!

1869
01:44:10,060 --> 01:44:12,860
You all did so wonderful!

1870
01:44:13,960 --> 01:44:17,460
ねぇ、ソフィー？
Hey, Sopia?

1871
01:44:17,560 --> 01:44:22,960
Yes! Oh my goodness, everybody, you were so great! And I just want to say thank you so much for coming.

1872
01:44:22,960 --> 01:44:27,160
本当に来てくれてありがとうございました！本当に楽しかった、マジで。
Thank you so much for coming! It was really fun, seriously.

1873
01:44:27,560 --> 01:44:35,460
最高！最高の Jump King イベントでしたから、みんなさんのおかげで、マジで最高！ありがとうございます！
It was the best! It was the best Jump King event, thanks to everyone! Seriously the best, thank you so much!

1874
01:44:34,860 --> 01:44:36,760
ありがとうございましたー！
Thank you very much!

1875
01:44:40,560 --> 01:44:41,560
Yay!

1876
01:44:40,960 --> 01:44:43,860
バーベキューやったー！ください！
BBQ, yay! Give it to us!

1877
01:44:43,060 --> 01:44:46,460
あれ、もらってない方が言ってますね。
Huh, someone who didn't win it is asking for it.

1878
01:44:46,160 --> 01:44:49,360
いやいやいや！行くから！連れて行くからな！
No no no! We're going! We'll take you along!

1879
01:44:50,060 --> 01:44:52,960
一緒に行きましょう！
Let me go together!

1880
01:44:52,860 --> 01:44:55,860
Good idea, いいアイデアですね！
Good idea, that's a good idea!

1881
01:44:55,860 --> 01:45:00,160
Yes! All right, if you didn't get up to the sewers and you didn't get a BBQ gift card...

1882
01:45:00,328 --> 01:45:03,968
I'm sure somebody will happily go with you...

1883
01:45:05,468 --> 01:45:09,668
楽しかったね。ありがとね、みんな。Thank you so much, and...
That was fun! Thank you so much, everybody, and...

1884
01:45:09,968 --> 01:45:15,968
これから、あの、ゆっくり休んでね。あの、このゲームはめっちゃむずいから... if the rage came out, well...
Please get some rest after this. This game is super tough, so if the rage came out, well...

1885
01:45:16,168 --> 01:45:20,668
ちょっと、怒ってる人ね、calm down and rest.
For anyone who got a bit angry, calm down and rest.

1886
01:45:21,168 --> 01:45:24,668
No more angry! Right, right.

1887
01:45:24,968 --> 01:45:28,668
すごい良く出来たから、本当に素晴らしい。You guys did amazing. So let's meet again soon.
You all did so well, truly amazing. You guys did amazing. So let's meet again soon.

1888
01:45:29,068 --> 01:45:31,168
Thank you so much for organizing!

1889
01:45:31,268 --> 01:45:32,568
You're welcome!

1890
01:45:32,668 --> 01:45:34,668
Thank you, guys!

1891
01:45:35,168 --> 01:45:40,168
私たち Jump King 大好きだからね。ちょっと、ちょっとヤバい人たちだからね。
We love Jump King, you see. We're a bit... a bit crazy like that.

1892
01:45:40,668 --> 01:45:43,168
Yeah, we love pain and suffering, so...

1893
01:45:43,668 --> 01:45:46,168
We love pain! We love pain!

1894
01:45:46,268 --> 01:45:47,968
I don't!

1895
01:45:49,968 --> 01:45:55,968
Only for today. Thank you so much, everybody, and let's end with 3, 2, 1, おつかれ...
Only for today. Thank you so much, everybody, and let's end with 3, 2, 1, otsukare...

1896
01:45:56,668 --> 01:46:00,168
おつ Jump King！ Okay, okay.
Otsu Jump King! Okay, okay.

1897
01:46:00,468 --> 01:46:05,668
Okay! はい！ 3, 2, 1, おつ Jump King!
Okay! Alright! 3, 2, 1, Otsu Jump King!

1898
01:46:06,168 --> 01:46:13,668
Bye bye!

1899
01:46:18,168 --> 01:46:21,168
よいしょ。聞こえるかな？
Yoisho. Can you hear me?

1900
01:46:21,668 --> 01:46:24,168
よいしょ、よいしょ、よいしょ。
Yoisho, yoisho, yoisho.

1901
01:46:24,368 --> 01:46:33,668
のじゃ！というわけで、おしまいなのですのじゃ！ありがとうございましたのじゃ！
Noja! So with that, it's over, noja! Thank you so much, noja!

1902
01:46:34,168 --> 01:46:44,368
なんと今回、ジャンプ準キング！準キングになった、2位になりましたのじゃ！ありがとうなのじゃ！
To my surprise, I came in 2nd place as the Jump Silver King, noja! Thank you, noja!

1903
01:46:44,668 --> 01:46:54,168
結構頑張った！わし結構頑張った！しかもなんかすごい良さそうなマッサージまで頂けるとのこと、すごい楽しみなのじゃ！
I worked really hard! I worked super hard! And I heard I'm getting a gift card for a really nice massage too, so I'm really looking forward to it, noja!

1904
01:46:54,668 --> 01:47:08,168
しかもね、アソビ★まわり隊ね、あの、キョーコも1位だったから、1位、2位、3位中2人がなんとルーキー！アソビ★まわり隊！すごい嬉しい！誇らしいのじゃ！やったのじゃ！のじゃ！
Plus, in Asobi☆Mawaritai!, Kyoko got 1st place! So out of 1st, 2nd, and 3rd, two of us are rookies from Asobi☆Mawaritai!! I'm so happy and proud, noja! Yay, noja!

1905
01:47:10,168 --> 01:47:15,668
嬉しい。キョーコとお隣なのも嬉しい。え、わしもここまで行けると思ってなかったよ。
I'm so happy. I'm glad to be right next to Kyoko too. I honestly didn't think I'd make it this far either.

1906
01:47:16,168 --> 01:47:23,168
わしもなんか、もっと下手くそだと思ってたけど、なんか意外といけた？なんか意外といけた？
I thought I'd be way worse at this, but I did surprisingly well, right? Unexpectedly well?

1907
01:47:24,168 --> 01:47:30,968
期待のルーキーかも。わしなんかゲーム...ゲームやれるかも。ゲーマーやれるかもしれない、もしかして。
Maybe I'm a promising rookie! I might actually... be good at gaming. Maybe I could be a real gamer!

1908
01:47:31,668 --> 01:47:36,168
ゲーマーの素質が...あるかもしれない。
I might have... true gamer potential.

1909
01:47:36,668 --> 01:47:44,168
あの、最後の方同心しちゃったけど...最後の方同心しちゃいましたけど、あの、これからね...
Well, I lost my focus a bit towards the very end... but from now on...

1910
01:47:44,368 --> 01:47:54,168
あの、色んなゲームにね、挑戦していこうと思っているので、うん。色んなゲームに挑戦していこうと思うので、頑張りますのじゃ！
Um, I plan to take on all kinds of different games, so yeah. I'll do my best with various games, noja!

1911
01:47:55,168 --> 01:48:06,168
Jump King も、あの、今日は全部クリア出来なかったけど、あの、耐久みたいな感じじゃなくて、ちょっとずつとかでもね、いつかやりたい...いつかやりたいなーって...
As for Jump King, I couldn't clear it all today, but instead of an endurance stream, I'd like to chip away at it little by little someday... I really hope to do that...

1912
01:48:06,368 --> 01:48:09,668
思惑ます。面白かったな！面白いゲームだった！
...I think. It was really fun! Such a fun game!

1913
01:48:09,768 --> 01:48:17,168
なんかその、なんじゃろ、あの、ゲ...ん？ Jump King のさ、あの、ゲームの...何て言うの？
You know, like... Jump King has that... what do you call it?

1914
01:48:17,668 --> 01:48:26,668
なんか二つ名じゃないけどさ、ってなんか割と鬼畜ゲーとかさ、なんかイライラして、なんか結構、あの、耐久ゲーとかさ、
Not a nickname exactly, but it has a reputation for being brutal, frustrating, or an endurance test...

1915
01:48:26,968 --> 01:48:32,168
そういうイメージだったけど、なんか意外と配信でやってみて、そんなことなかったな。
That's the image I had, but actually trying it on stream, it wasn't really like that at all.

1916
01:48:32,368 --> 01:48:39,668
意外とそんなことなかった。なんか、そんなイライラしなかったな、配信中は。配信中はそんなイライラしなかったのじゃ。
Surprisingly not at all. I didn't really get frustrated during the stream. On stream, I didn't get mad at all, noja.

1917
01:48:40,168 --> 01:48:44,968
1人でやってた時は「うにゃー」ってなってたけど...うん。
When I was practicing alone, I was all "Aaaaagh!", but... yeah.

1918
01:48:45,168 --> 01:48:54,668
なんか落ちても「あー、まあじゃあそこまで行くか。まあじゃあそこまで行くか」みたいな気持ちで、冷静に出来た。素質があるかもしれない。うん。
Even when I fell, I just calmly thought, "Ah well, let's just climb back up there." Maybe I really do have the aptitude for it! Yeah.

1919
01:48:57,168 --> 01:49:03,168
楽しかったよ、わしやってて。なんかその、あんま苦しみはなかったかも。あ、耐久じゃないからかな？
I had fun playing it. I didn't feel much suffering. Ah, maybe because it wasn't an endurance challenge?

1920
01:49:03,368 --> 01:49:15,668
最初から、最初からなんかこの、なんじゃろな...耐久をやります、絶対にクリアするまで配信を終わりません！みたいな感じの...
If I had framed it from the start like, "This is an endurance stream, I won't end until I clear it!"...

1921
01:49:15,968 --> 01:49:24,168
そういう名目でやってたら結構キツかったじゃろうけど、あの、耐久配信じゃなくて、その、どこまで上まで行けるか、みたいな、そういう...
If I had approached it under those conditions, it probably would have been rough, but instead of endurance, it was just "How high can you climb?"...

1922
01:49:24,368 --> 01:49:32,168
企画コンセプトが良かったね！今回の、あの、先輩が開催してくださった、そのエンジョイ...初心者向けエンジョイ向け大会、みたいなののコンセプトが...
The event concept was great! The concept set up by our seniors for this beginner-friendly casual tournament...

1923
01:49:32,368 --> 01:49:41,168
その、クリアしなきゃいけない、じゃなくて、どこまで行けるかな、みたいな、そういう、しかもその時間も1時間ですって決まった上でやってたから、
...wasn't "You must clear it," but "Let's see how far you can go," and with a set 1-hour time limit...

1924
01:49:41,368 --> 01:49:45,668
その、苦しまずに、なんか「あ、このゲームおもろいな」と思いながら...そう。
...so without suffering, I could play thinking, "Ah, this game is fun!" Yeah.

1925
01:49:46,168 --> 01:49:59,168
なんか「苦しいな」とか「しんどいな」とか「全然上手く出来ないな」とか、イライラするというよりも、なんか「どこまで行けるかな」みたいな気持ちで出来たから...うん、すごいプレイしやすかった！すごい良い企画！
Rather than feeling frustrated like "This is painful," or "This is tough," or "I'm so bad at this," I could play with the mindset of "I wonder how far I can get!" So yeah, it was really easy to play! Such a great event!

1926
01:50:00,176 --> 01:50:01,476
良かったのう。
I'm so glad.

1927
01:50:01,476 --> 01:50:04,456
うん、そう、プレッシャーなくてね、そうそうそうそう。
Yeah, there was no pressure, right? Exactly.

1928
01:50:04,456 --> 01:50:10,076
すごいね、なんか、あの、なんじゃろ、苦しみゲーと思われがちなゲームを...
It's amazing... like, a game that's usually thought of as a rage game...

1929
01:50:10,076 --> 01:50:15,536
で、わしもそう思ってたけど、外から見てて。そうなんのかなと思ってたけど、
...and I thought so too watching from the outside. I wondered if it really was,

1930
01:50:15,536 --> 01:50:26,676
意外とやってみると、なんかそのやり方？耐久じゃなかったりとか、こういう、今回の大会の形式みたいな感じの...
but when you actually play it, like with this format? When it's not an endurance stream, and it's set up like this tournament...

1931
01:50:26,676 --> 01:50:31,876
やり方だとすごい楽しめた。チルゲーかは分かんないけど、チルゲーかは分かんなかったけど、うん。
...I really enjoyed playing it this way. I didn't know if it'd feel chill, but yeah.

1932
01:50:31,876 --> 01:50:35,576
すごいね、なんか楽しいゲームだなと思って。
I realized it's actually a really fun game!

1933
01:50:36,176 --> 01:50:40,576
プレイできて、すごい良かった。すごい良かったのじゃ。
I'm really glad I got to play it. Really glad!

1934
01:50:41,176 --> 01:50:44,976
企画が良かったね。うん、ありがたいのじゃ。
The event structure was great. Yeah, I'm so grateful.

1935
01:50:45,476 --> 01:50:50,976
改めて、カリオペ先輩とリオナ先輩、企画を準備してくださってありがとうございます。
Once again, Calliope-senpai and Riona-senpai, thank you so much for organizing this event.

1936
01:50:51,176 --> 01:50:57,776
すごい楽しい、楽しくジャンプキングを遊ばせていただきましたのじゃ！
I had so much fun playing Jump King!

1937
01:50:58,376 --> 01:51:02,176
うん。じゃあ、そろそろ配信おしまいにしようかな。
Alright. I think I'll wrap up the stream soon.

1938
01:51:02,176 --> 01:51:08,676
あ！そうだ、あの、明日アンデッドの歌ってみたを投稿するのじゃ！しますのじゃ！
Oh! That's right! Tomorrow I'm releasing a cover of "UNDEAD"! Yes, I am!

1939
01:51:09,476 --> 01:51:17,676
そして、あの、ちらっと、動画もちらっと、チラ見せ公開みたいなのTwitterでしているので、そちらもあのリツイートとかね、
And I've posted a short sneak peek video on Twitter, so please feel free to retweet it...

1940
01:51:19,576 --> 01:51:22,476
いいねとかね、うん、お願いします。
...like it, and all that! Please check it out.

1941
01:51:22,476 --> 01:51:33,376
そして、あのジャンプキング大会と同時期になんと、アソビ★まわり隊！の初めての公式番組が始まっておりましたので、おぬしらそちらもぜひ！そちらもぜひご覧くださいのじゃ！
And at the same time as this Jump King tournament, Asobi★Mawaritai!'s very first official show has started, so everyone, please check that out as well!

1942
01:51:33,376 --> 01:51:38,376
そちらもぜひご覧ください。ちょっとレイドしとくか。次、次の公式番組に飛ばすか、おぬしらを。
Please be sure to watch it! Should I raid them? Should I raid the official program next?

1943
01:51:44,376 --> 01:51:46,676
あれ？のじゃ？いけるか？
Huh? Wait? Can I do it?

1944
01:51:47,176 --> 01:51:52,376
うん、おぬしらを次の行き先をそこにしようかな。
Yeah, maybe I'll make that the next destination for you guys.

1945
01:51:52,376 --> 01:52:00,976
アソビ★まわり隊！の「みんなでアソバッニ」飛ばそうかな。飛ばせるかな？飛ばせるのかな？
Maybe I'll raid Asobi★Mawaritai!'s "Minna de Asoban-ni". Can I raid it? Can I send you there?

1946
01:52:00,976 --> 01:52:07,676
ライブしか飛ばせない？動画飛ばせないのかな？ライブって飛ばせないのかな？
Can you only raid live streams? You can't raid videos? Wait, can you not raid videos?

1947
01:52:07,676 --> 01:52:11,676
飛ばせないか？飛ばせないか？
You can't? You can't raid it?

1948
01:52:11,676 --> 01:52:17,476
あ、動画ダメなの？動画ダメ...あ、動画ダメっぽい。
Ah, videos don't work? Videos... Ah, looks like videos don't work.

1949
01:52:18,176 --> 01:52:24,576
プレミア公開とかはいけるけど、動画無理っぽいのじゃ。ちょっと動画無理っぽいから、あの、あきらめてアンデッドに飛ばすか。
You can raid Premieres, but normal videos seem impossible. Since videos won't work, maybe I'll give up and send you to "UNDEAD" instead?

1950
01:52:24,576 --> 01:52:31,376
あきらめてアンデッドに飛ばして、高評価をおねだりするか。このまま高評価をおぬしらにしてもらうとするか。
I'll give up and raid "UNDEAD", and beg for likes! I'll just ask you guys to go like it right now.

1951
01:52:31,876 --> 01:52:33,376
残念。
Too bad.

1952
01:52:33,376 --> 01:52:40,976
それではあの後ほどちゃんとリツイートもしますので、そちらで、あの、アソビ★まわり隊！の動画と歌ってみたをご覧くだいさい！
Anyway, I'll retweet it later, so please check out both the Asobi★Mawaritai! video and my cover song from there!

1953
01:52:41,176 --> 01:52:46,976
お楽しみにー！それでは、今日の配信はおしまいなんのじゃー！
Look forward to it! And with that, today's stream is coming to an end!

1954
01:52:47,176 --> 01:52:50,676
おぬしら、さらばじゃー！
Everyone, farewell!

